 ## Summary
 
+The required `tool/parsed-call` event uses the existing Tool Conversation Definition and public records. Parsed object arguments remain distinct from raw `tool/call` strings through dispatch, final result and replay. Assistant model blocks remain raw-only. The producer must establish authoritative owner/context association before emitting either call representation; matching a public call ID here does not establish Native ownership after reopen.
+
 Generation-scoped Conversation replacement retires old row identities, history-navigation callbacks, image reads, scroll anchors, and disclosure choices. Reused numeric turn or answer positions cannot inherit choices from another projection. Rebuilding and failure use the existing history status presentation; retained execution scopes and pending Interactions keep their lifetimes.
 
 Use this package to render a browser chat from recorded Session conversations, including historical images, localized actions, and restored scroll position. Work-details modes control reasoning previews and process visibility without hiding Assistant replies; Verbose keeps completed-turn process rows visible. Local transcript and steering submissions appear immediately, remain in their original surface, and disappear atomically when authoritative Session records arrive, while queued submissions stay outside Chat. The package does not assemble or modify model requests.
